\viewkind4\uc1\pard\tx3780\tx3960\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Our blest Redeemer, ere He breathed
\par His tender last farewell,
\par A Guide, a Comforter bequeathed,
\par With us to dwell.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. He came in semblance of a dove,
\par With sheltering wings outspread,
\par The holy balm of peace and love
\par On each to shed.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. He came in tongues of living flame,
\par To teach, convince of living flame,
\par To teach, convince, subdue;
\par All-powerful as the wind He came,
\par As viewless too.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. He comes sweet influence to impart,
\par A gracious, willing guest,
\par While He can find one humble heart
\par Wherein to rest.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. And His that gentle voice we hear,
\par Soft as the breath of even,
\par That checks each fault, that calms each fear,
\par And speaks of heaven.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. And every virtue we possess,
\par And every conquest won,
\par And every thought of holiness,
\par Are His alone.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 7\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 7. Spirit of purity and grace,
\par Our weakness, pitying, see;
\par O make our hearts Thy dwelling-place,
\par And worthier Thee.\i 
\par \pard\i0               Amen.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2 
\par }

